[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Fourth Reference Slice - Nonlinear Diode Operating Points

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Iterations 151-200 introduced a bounded Shockley diode and analytic damped Newton DC operating points. Later bounded extensions add AC bias linearization and backward-Euler nonlinear transient stepping. This slice does not qualify semiconductor model parity, model plugins, general nonlinear integration methods, or production convergence guarantees.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REF4-001
TITLE: Validated diode model and conventions
STATEMENT: >>>
The reference engine shall represent a two-terminal Shockley diode with positive finite saturation current and thermal voltage, with terminal current defined from p to n.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/circuit.rs, src/model.rs.
Verification: tests/nonlinear.rs::shockley_diode_has_positive_incremental_conductance, tests/nonlinear.rs::diode_circuit_parameters_are_validated_at_the_public_boundary.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-MOD-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REF4-011
TITLE: Shockley derivative qualification
STATEMENT: >>>
The bounded diode model shall expose a parameter-validation operation and provide an analytic incremental conductance equal, within a documented finite-difference tolerance, to the derivative of its p-to-n Shockley current throughout the accepted finite evaluation domain. This requirement qualifies the implemented diode Jacobian only; it does not claim a general semiconductor-model framework or vendor model parity.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/model.rs::DiodeModel::validate and linearize. Verification: tests/nonlinear.rs::seeded_shockley_jacobian_matches_finite_difference.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REF4-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REF4-002
TITLE: Analytic bounded Newton operating point
STATEMENT: >>>
The reference engine shall solve diode operating points using an analytic residual and Jacobian, bounded line-search damping, finite trial checks and explicit iteration/tolerance limits.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/newton.rs, src/dc.rs.
Verification: tests/nonlinear.rs::forward_biased_resistor_diode_bias_point_converges, tests/nonlinear.rs::high_bias_diode_uses_bounded_damping_instead_of_exponential_overflow, tests/nonlinear.rs::Newton_iteration_budget_is_a_real_failure_boundary.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-EQ-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REF4-003
TITLE: Explicit nonlinear analysis capability boundaries
STATEMENT: >>>
The reference engine shall form nonlinear AC from a converged DC bias and analytic diode incremental conductances, and shall solve diode transient requests only through the bounded backward-Euler Newton path. Unsupported nonlinear transient methods shall fail explicitly. Successful nonlinear operating points shall expose Newton evidence.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/ac.rs, src/transient.rs, src/configured.rs, src/newton.rs and src/api.rs.
Verification: tests/nonlinear.rs::nonlinear_ac_linearizes_at_the_dc_bias_point, tests/nonlinear.rs::nonlinear_backward_euler_transient_produces_finite_committed_samples, tests/nonlinear.rs::configured_backward_euler_accepts_nonlinear_diode_steps and configured-method rejection cases.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REF-003

